  "region_definition": "Footprint: 2D convex hull of the existing active collision mesh projected onto sensor-body local XY. Outward direction: sensor-body local +Z (thin sensor normal). Minimum Z: lowest vertex on an outward-facing pad hull facet with normal dot +Z >= 0.5, minus 0.5 mm observation-only margin. Maximum Z: greatest parent collision vertex Z in the same sensor-body frame plus 0.5 mm observation-only margin. Thus existing broad parent convex hull contacts over a buried pad can activate its channel without moving or creating collision geometry. The runtime should additionally reject side/back contacts using the outward normal direction. These are virtual localized contact regions, not a pressure/deformation or load-transfer model.",
